{"created": "2025-05-08T17:14:15.407310+00:00", "modified": "2025-05-22T19:35:46.243189+00:00", "id": 15367103, "conceptrecid": "15367102", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.15367103", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.15367102", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.15367103", "metadata": {"title": "tairaeli/Metagalactic_Ultraviolet_Background_Data_Tables: Ultraviolet Background Data Table Reformat", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.15367103", "publication_date": "2025-05-08", "description": "<p>Much of the observed ion abundances within the Circumgalactic Medium (CGM) is poorly understood. One of the key features of the CGM that contributes to this is the ultraviolet background (UVB). A large number of models have been created over the years to characterize this background radiation based on the latest observational data. As such, the formatting between models has not remained consistent. This data release reformatts several widely used models (<a href=\"https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/2009ApJ...703.1416F/abstract\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Faucher-Gigu&egrave;re 2009</a>, <a href=\"https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/2012ApJ...746..125H/abstract\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Haardt and Madau 2012</a>, <a href=\"https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/2019MNRAS.485...47P/abstract\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Puchwein et al 2019</a>, and <a href=\"https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/2020MNRAS.493.1614F/abstract\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Faucher-Gigu&egrave;re 2020</a>). Additionally, it also provides code for usage with <a href=\"https://github.com/brittonsmith/cloudy_cooling_tools\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">cloudy_cooling_tools</a>, with scripts to convert data to a usable cloudy input, along with code to run &nbsp;cloudy_cooling_tools. Note: this code does not come with a working installation of<a href=\"https://github.com/brittonsmith/cloudy_cooling_tools\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"> cloudy_cooling_tools</a>. Information on installing 